<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ ADRs firmer as Dow soars over 6000 mark.</title>
<headline>NZ ADRs firmer as Dow soars over 6000 mark.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand ADRs were firmer in New York on Tuesday as the Dow Industrials soared 40.25 to 6009.63 in late trade.</p>
<p>Price movements of NZ stocks listed in the U.S., Britain and</p>
<p>Australia.</p>
<p>Company	Exchange    Last	  Net change</p>
<p>Tranz Rail     N.Y.    US$14 1/8	 +0 1/4</p>
<p>FCL Bldg	 N.Y.    US$25 7/8	 +0 5/8</p>
<p>FCL Engy	 N.Y.    US$26 1/4	 +0 3/4</p>
<p>FCL Paper	N.Y.    US$20	     +0 1/4</p>
<p>FCL Forest     N.Y.    US$16	     +0 1/2</p>
<p>Telecom	  N.Y.    US$78 1/4	 +1 1/2</p>
<p>Guinness Peat  London  35		  -0 1/2</p>
<p>Brierley	 London  64		 untraded</p>
<p>NZ IT	    London  235		 +1</p>
<p>Foreign &amp; Col  London  155 1/2	   +1</p>
<p>Templeton	London  139 1/4	   +0 1/2</p>
<p>Lion	     Sydney  A$3.15	    +5</p>
<p>Goodman	  Sydney  A$1.48	    +4</p>
<p>Macraes	  Sydney  A$3.15	    nil</p>
<p>Notes - In New York, Telecom's American Depository Receipts are traded in bundles of 16 shares, while both the Fletcher Challenge shares are in bundles of 10 each. Tranz Rail ADSs are groups of three ordinary shares.</p>
<p>- London prices are mid-rates.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
